--   The numeric consequences of the budget.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegJPre1`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.segReg_num (h : SegReg P R s t lam w α) :
--       200 * (3 * (lam : ℝ) + 1) ≤ 2 ^ P ∧
--       100 * (((lam : ℝ) + 1) * (3 * lam + 3) + 1) ≤ 2 ^ P ∧
--       (lam : ℝ) * (2 * w + 1) * (15 * ddR (α : ℝ) ((t : ℝ) / s) (lam - 1) *
--         (((lam : ℝ) + 1) * (3 * lam + 3) + 1) / 2 ^ P) ≤ 1 / 100 ∧
--       8 * ((s : ℝ) + 1) ^ 2 ≤ 2 ^ P ∧ 1 ≤ P
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** `J` kernel precondition (JPre), part 1: the regime and the capacitance of a line
--
--   `SegReg P R s t λ w α` bundles the hypotheses of `segInvFullS_err` (with `Bu = 1/2`, as used by
--   `B0seg`): `0 < s ≤ t`, `2 ≤ α`, `3 ≤ xθ`, `1 ≤ λ`, `w ≤ s`, `D_{λ-1} ≤ 2^R`,
--   `1000 · fullG λ w s t α (1/2) ≤ 2^P`.
--
--   `segReg_cap`: in this regime the capacitance `capI P (TT P R s t α) (BB s t λ w)` on the line
--   `LJ s t λ w` has row sums `|C/2^P - I| ≤ η ≤ 1/4`, vanishes off the pattern
--   `bandS (λ+w) (s-λ-w)`, and `(|LJ|+1)²/2^P ≤ 1/8` (so also `η + |LJ|²/2^P ≤ 1/2`).
